 "‘Rank 1,2,3, not JKT’: Two lowest vote-earning Republicans unite to try and give GOP best shot at winning governor’s race", "source": "Alaska's News Source", "published": "2026-09-25T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 2.09, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 7.38, "poll_sd": 9.79, "poll_weight": 0.23, "fundamentals": {"margin": 0.07, "lean": -4.5, "environment": 4.1, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 0.47}, "rating_margin": 3.43, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.38, "baseline_margin": 3.3, "analyst_adjustment": 2.2, "key_factors": ["Republican field is fractured: Trump endorsed Wilson while Taylor refused calls to exit and Bronson stayed in, risking a split GOP vote under ranked-choice tabulation", "Kreiss-Tomkins has raised $2.1M, more than double all three Republicans combined", "Ratings momentum toward Democrats: Cook and Sabato moved to Lean D flip, Silver Bulletin to Likely D, and markets price a Democratic win near 80-85%", "Alaska's R+6 lean, Republican-sponsored polls showing a closer race, and sparse polling cap how far the forecast can move"], "rationale": "Kreiss-Tomkins holds a clear fundraising lead and recent surveys put him at 52-54%, while the Republican side is divided by Trump's endorsement of Wilson over the better-funded Taylor. Raters and prediction markets have shifted toward Democrats, but the state's Republican lean and thin polling keep this at Lean D rather than stronger.", "watch": "If Taylor, Wilson, and Bronson consolidate behind a single Republican before the ranked-choice general, the race would tighten quickly.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike Dunleavy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alaska's governorship is open as Republican Mike Dunleavy terms out, and the race to replace him tilts toward Democrat Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins. Recent surveys put him at 52 to 54 percent against the Republican field, and he has raised about $2.1 million, more than double the three Republicans combined. Treg Taylor leads Republican fundraising but has drawn fire within his party after refusing Donald Trump's call to exit; Trump instead endorsed Bernadette Wilson, while Dave Bronson remains in the race.\n\nRaters have moved the contest toward Democrats, with Cook and Sabato calling it a Lean D flip and markets pricing a Democratic win near 80 percent. Still, Alaska leans Republican by about six points, Republican-sponsored polls show a closer contest, and polling is sparse. A fractured Republican field could still consolidate, which would make this a genuinely close finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6825, "margin": 2.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7395, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7331, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7071, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7365, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7204, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7496, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7614, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7414, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7728, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7784, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7949, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8004, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7839, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.7591, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.7654, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.7464, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.7725,